WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.534
First, let me just ask

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.235
how you're feeling.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.970
You have finished cancer treatment.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.071
Yes. You're in remission.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.007
Yes. And I got a clean bill of health.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.675
Amazing. I'm in remission.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.676
They can't find any cancer.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:09.943
Cells,

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.611
so I'm waiting for my hair

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.780
and my eyelashes and everything

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:14.547
come back.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.181
Fantastic.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:15.882
Well, it's important

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:16.616
that you're feeling better.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.051
That's great news.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.686
Let's talk about your reaction

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.888
to CNN's reporting this week

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.189
that federal prosecutors

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.524
have an audio recording

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.892
of the former president

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.893
talking about

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.462
holding on to classified documents.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:32.098
At least one about a potential U.S.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.333
attack on Iran.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.668
He had that after he left office.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.037
Do you think this tape could be

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.071
a smoking gun?

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.572
Well, apparently the recording

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.942
also reflects Donald Trump's knowledge

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:46.579
that he had not declassified

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:47.080
the document.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.516
So he knew that it was still classified.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.350
And that's

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.019
an additional element of importance to

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.154
this recording.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.689
And can you

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.025
explain why that's an additional Well,

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:00.760
for a while at least,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.162
there was a halfhearted effort

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:05.131
to claim by Donald Trump that he could

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.367
just magically declassify

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.203
you know, telepathically or mentally.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.407
And this seems to reflect his clear

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.609
understanding that he had not

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.078
declassified this document

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.679
and that it was still classified.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.447
And so

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.515
the document is missing at this point,

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:23.716
as I understand it,

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.585
according to published reports.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.454
Do you believe, based on this

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:27.854
and of course,

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:28.421
everything else

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.522
that you've seen,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.124
that the former president

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.393
should be charged, criminally charged?

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.127
I mean, that's

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.261
obviously a

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.130
decision for the Department of Justice

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.199
and for a grand jury.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.200
But

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.670
the I mean, these charges are

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.504
very serious.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.905
I mean, the allegations

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:46.973
that he took

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:47.841
all of these documents,

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:50.009
including top secret documents,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.212
and then didn't return them

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.279
and deliberately withheld

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.380
them are very serious.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:54.814
I mean,

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.583
I don't think any president

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.584
has ever been accused

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.119
of doing anything like that before.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:02.222
And just quickly, how much does the fact

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.924
that he clearly in this tape

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.293
suggest that he knows that he can't,

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:07.760
as you

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.796
get to your words, magically declassify?

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.830
How much does that play

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.398
into the DOJ's case?

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.133
Well, a lot,

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:16.736
because I think a key ingredient in

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.371
determining the intent

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.839
with which a person acts

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.541
is consciousness of guilt.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:24.744
And if a person acts with consciousness

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:25.612
of their own guilt

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:26.846
or consciousness,

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.848
of their own potential wrongdoing,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.883
that demonstrates

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:32.185
that if they go forward, nonetheless,

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.453
there's intent. And,

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.188
you know, my

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.055
understanding is

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.590
is that there were hundreds

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.958
of documents taken.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.460
Many of them were classified.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.629
Some of them were Top-Secret secret,

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.931
and yet they were deliberately withheld.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:47.433
And if the prosecutor, Jack Smith,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.135
has information to that effect,

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.703
that's a very serious business.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.671
I want to ask about something

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:52.305
that you're dealing

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.374
with on the Oversight Committee.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.075
Republican Chairman

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:56.676
who worked with,

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.043
of course,

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:57.710
James Comey,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.612
said he will hold the FBI

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.014
director, Chris Wray,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:01.881
in contempt

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.750
over an FBI document

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.952
containing and unsubstantial

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.587
created bribery allegations

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.923
involving then-Vice President Joe Biden.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.358
Wray offered to let you in Comber

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.693
view the document

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.995
and do it in a secure location.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:16.763
Comber wants it

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.331
physically turned over

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.465
to the full committee.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.266
What are your thoughts?

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.267
You're the ranking Democrat

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:21.734
on that committee.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.270
So the FBI is coming tomorrow

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.240
to show Chairman Komar and me

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.209
the document that they're looking for.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:29.943
In other words,

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.745
the Republican majority

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.480
in the committee is getting everything

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.082
they're asking for.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.450
In terms of seeing the document,

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.151
which, by the way,

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:40.887
they say they have also already seen,

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:42.989
and yet they're still talking

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.790
about holding

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.559
the director of the FBI in contempt,

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.361
even though they're getting exactly

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.095
what they want.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.030
Even though the FBI has been

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.732
overwhelmingly cooperative

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.969
and accommodating to this request.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:57.737
So that demonstrates to me

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.572
that what they're really interested in

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.040
is in holding

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.243
the FBI director in contempt,

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.777
not in getting a document

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.346
that they've already seen.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.046
And, you know,

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.348
I don't know what this document is

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:11.117
because the majority has closed us out.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.052
The Democrats on the committee,

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.121
they are no longer

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.956
respecting a bipartisan agreement

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.091
that the committees had

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:18.858
for the last several.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.493
Congress have no idea what's in it.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.795
Well, there have been published reports

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:24.631
which suggest that

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.432
it has to do with Ukraine.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.834
That was a period, remember,

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.003
when Rudy Giuliani was running around

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:34.407
with a Russian agent who later was found

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.509
to be sold by the Treasury Department,

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.378
Trump's Treasury Department,

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.813
and he was waving different kinds

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:41.781
of documents.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.516
Attorney General Barr,

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.550
Trump's own attorney

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.186
general, was so skeptical that he created

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:47.820
a panel

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.522
to look at all of this information,

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:49.789
saying

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.324
you've got to take the Ukraine stuff

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.225
with a grain of salt.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.427
So I think it probably has to do

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:57.597
with Ukraine and allegations

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:58.731
that went nowhere.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:04:59.265
In other words,

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.301
this was looked at by the Trump

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.402
Justice Department,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.470
and I think they ended all of it

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.506
in August with no prosecutions,

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:07.307
no indictments,

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.542
and they're going back to recycle

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.678
these unfounded accusations.

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.579
Let's go back to the initial question

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.715
about how much access

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.717
the Congress will get to this document,

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.419
whether you can actually have it.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.287
If the roles were reversed

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.189
and you found out that

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.624
the FBI had a document

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:25.858
containing an allegation

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.060
about Donald Trump, wouldn't

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.394
you want unfettered access

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:29.362
to that document?

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:30.463
Well, of course, you always want

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:31.230
unfettered access.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.065
But remember,

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:32.932
you're talking to somebody

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.701
who was in the majority

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:35.902
when Donald Trump was president,

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:38.938
when he ordered every Department of U.S.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:39.572
government

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:40.773
not to comply in

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:41.808
any way

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.710
with requests of the House

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.744
Oversight Committee.

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.512
So it would have been remarkable

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.514
if every time we requested the document,

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:50.683
they brought it over to show it to us,

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.318
much less give it to us.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.520
So they keep changing the demand

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.856
in order to find some reason

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.091
to find fault

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:59.592
with the FBI Director Wray,

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.626
which is why I say

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.328
what they're really going after

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.297
is a contempt citation against him.

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:06.065
And it's all part of what Chairman

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:06.966
Colmer

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.768
admitted was an effort

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:11.003
to get Donald Trump's poll numbers up.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.206
It's all about the 20, 24 campaign.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.874
Let me ask you something

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.310
about what happened this past week

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:17.910
where you work

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:18.978
in the House of Representatives,

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.179
Congress in general, the debt

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.681
ceiling deal

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:23.716
The president said that

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.918
Kevin McCarthy worked in good faith.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.620
Do you give him credit

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.789
for this bipartisan deal?

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.758
The president that excuse me,

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.626
Kevin McCarthy, the speaker.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:36.195
Well, look, there is mega

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.730
extreme elements

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.732
within the Republican caucus

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.868
which really wanted to plunge the country

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:44.337
into default, an economic crisis.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.773
That's the chaos caucus.

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:48.207
I mean, these are the same people

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:49.642
that supported Donald Trump's.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:51.310
What about Kevin McCarthy? Because he's.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:51.711
Well, right.

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:52.211
So, yeah,

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.447
but I'm distinguishing him from them.

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:55.047
I think

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:55.982
he recognized

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.750
and he listened to the voices

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.651
on Wall Street

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.153
and in corporate America

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:02.989
who said you cannot crash the economy

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:06.392
just because you have an extreme element

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.693
that is heckling

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:09.762
you and hectoring you to do that.

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.497
And so in that sense,

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:12.298
the center

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:13.933
held briefly

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:16.102
because we were able to avert

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.303
going over the cliff,

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:19.338
but we should never come remotely close

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:20.072
to that again.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.841
The Constitution says

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:24.143
that the validity of the public debt

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.912
shall never be questioned.

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:27.780
That's in the 14th Amendment.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.015
Should that be change?

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.683
Well, I know you know, the answer

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:32.685
is you think the Constitution

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.921
already establishes a backstop

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.389
against what they wanted to do.

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:37.356
But I think, yes,

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.491
having a debt ceiling

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.226
statute is a threat to us

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:41.861
because they will keep trying

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:44.330
to careen the whole country over a cliff.

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:45.798
A few other topics

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:46.933
I want to get to first.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:47.900
You saw, I'm sure,

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.836
what happened at the Air Force

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.070
Academy this past week.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.573
President Biden tripped over a sandbag.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.108
He fell hard on the stage.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:56.809
He says, over

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:57.376
and over

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:59.245
to people concerned about his age.

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:00.847
Watch me now.

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:01.848
We want to be clear.

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:03.783
He wasn't hurt, which is great.

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:04.884
Also want to be clear,

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:06.552
presidents have tripped.

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:07.520
Everybody trips.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.455
I've tripped you've probably tripped.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:12.124
But we also know you've never tripped.

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:12.692
Okay.

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:14.160
But you also, as a politician

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.262
know about how events

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:17.730
feed into a perception

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.432
that already exists.

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:20.433
Questions about his

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:21.334
age are already there.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:23.903
Are voters wrong to

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:25.171
be worried about reelecting

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:25.571
a man

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:26.806
who would be closer

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:27.540
to 90

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.909
at the end of his second term than 80?

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:30.476
You know,

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:32.678
America is a country that loves youth

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:33.813
and vitality, you know,

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:34.814
which is why we have laws

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:36.449
against age discrimination,

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:38.284
because we tend to favor,

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:39.452
favor youthfulness.

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:42.255
And the new thing in a lot of countries,

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:43.823
people who've been in office

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:45.658
a longer period of time are praised

00:08:45.658 --> 00:08:46.526
for their wisdom.

00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:48.661
And I think that Joe Biden rightly

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:51.230
says that he has grown very wise

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.598
in his many decades

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:55.401
in public office, and I respect that.

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.603
So I think that he deserves to be judged

00:08:57.603 --> 00:08:58.838
by the results

00:08:58.838 --> 00:08:59.972
of his administration

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.140
and what he's gotten done

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:01.641
in terms

00:09:01.641 --> 00:09:04.911
of a bipartisan infrastructure law.

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:06.846
The Inflation Reduction Act

00:09:06.846 --> 00:09:08.447
lowering prescription drug prices,

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:09.682
I mean, really, that's

00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:12.251
what should matter to us as the people

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:14.220
you have a decision to make,

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.388
and that is whether or not

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:18.324
you are going to run for Senate

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:21.093
and in Maryland for Ben Cardin seat,

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:22.395
he is retiring.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:23.195
Have you decided

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:24.497
are you going to run for Senate?

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:25.631
I've not decided.

00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:26.332
I you know,

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:28.000
I love the House of Representatives.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.535
I love the people I serve with

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:31.037
and I love being in the people's House.

00:09:31.037 --> 00:09:33.306
But as some of my House

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:34.440
colleagues have pointed out,

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.375
these Senate seats only open up

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:38.010
every 25 or 30 years.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.712
A lot of people are encouraging me

00:09:39.712 --> 00:09:40.713
to check it out

00:09:40.713 --> 00:09:42.081
because there are certain

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:43.049
constitutional functions

00:09:43.049 --> 00:09:44.717
the Senate has that the House doesn't

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:45.484
have, like advice

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:48.087
and consent, Supreme Court nominations,

00:09:48.287 --> 00:09:49.755
judicial confirmations,

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:51.123
a lot of things that I'm interested in,

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:51.991
and that's why

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:53.526
I'm seriously considering it.

00:09:53.526 --> 00:09:54.393
But I've not decided.

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:55.161
When will you decide

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:56.896
I'm hoping

00:09:56.896 --> 00:09:58.097
before the 4th of July

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.999
I will have an answer for everybody.

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:01.667
The election's not until May.

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:03.035
24th. 20, 24.

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:04.670
So it's still 11 months away.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:05.171
The primary

00:10:05.171 --> 00:10:06.639
and then the election is a year

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:06.973
and a half.

00:10:06.973 --> 00:10:09.642
Your fellow Marylander, Steny Hoyer,

00:10:09.642 --> 00:10:11.644
who is a leader of your party

00:10:11.644 --> 00:10:12.244
for a long time,

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:13.446
you endorsed a different candidate.

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:14.780
Will that affect your decision?

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.116
Well, obviously you're my friend.

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:18.551
And so I've talked to him.

00:10:18.551 --> 00:10:18.884
I've talked

00:10:18.884 --> 00:10:20.453
to all of my colleagues about it.

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:21.854
I mean, we've got awesome

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:24.090
political leaders in Maryland and

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:27.193
I would not run against anybody else.

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:27.793
I mean, it's

00:10:27.793 --> 00:10:29.895
totally based on the experience

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:32.331
I've had trying to defend our democracy

00:10:32.331 --> 00:10:33.065
and our freedom

00:10:33.065 --> 00:10:34.467
and the bill of rights

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:36.569
against the Trump movement,

00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:38.004
which I think is like the death sentence,

00:10:38.004 --> 00:10:38.571
like you're

00:10:38.571 --> 00:10:39.271
you're getting ready

00:10:39.271 --> 00:10:41.774
for your campaign message there.

00:10:41.774 --> 00:10:42.541
Well,

00:10:43.109 --> 00:10:44.777
I suppose you can never be too ready,

00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:46.646
but I really haven't decided in there

00:10:46.646 --> 00:10:48.648
compelling reasons on both sides

00:10:48.648 --> 00:10:50.082
that my constituents

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:52.051
are presenting me with on a daily basis.

00:10:52.051 --> 00:10:53.185
And I love hearing from people.

00:10:53.185 --> 00:10:53.853
Congressman,

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:54.920
thank you so much for coming in.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.722
And again, such great news

00:10:56.722 --> 00:10:57.423
about your recovery.

00:10:57.423 --> 00:10:58.624
You're very kind. Thank you, Dana.

